      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TEABISCUIT (6) is the top pick despite being below market expectation at Collie, where he was favourite and raced wide when fifth in a BM56+. His previous Moora fourth came in BM64+ grade, and the drop into a BM52+ with a proven 1190m profile, plus a win from two starts at this track, gives him the right platform to rebound. ADDICTIVE DREAM (2) brings the best winning form, having taken a BM56+ at Leinster by just over half a length after working into the race neatly, and her three wins from five starts this season keep her very much in the argument. RIVER ANGEL (4) is better judged on the Collie second as a well-supported favourite than the Bunbury eighth, where she raced wide throughout in Class 3 company, so she is a sound place chance if she runs back to that earlier effort. STORM LORD (3) also gets relief from stronger company after a wide run at Belmont Park in Class 5 grade and holds minor claims.",
